# Categories ADDED to the original 28 Deutsch Well (2023) categories — v0.2 modifications.
# Each addition covers a high-volume theme in the QA corpus that the 2023 vault predates or omits.
# One JSON object per line: {"label", "definition", "topics": [slugs], "rationale"}
# Delete a line and rebuild to reject an addition; the original 28 are never touched by this file.
{"label": "Quantum Physics and the Multiverse", "definition": "Quantum theory taken seriously as a description of reality: the multiverse, interference, fungibility, and the physics underlying information and computation.", "topics": ["physics", "multiverse", "quantum", "quantum-multiverse", "quantum-gravity", "wave-function-collapse", "physics-history", "physic-history"], "rationale": "physics (161 QA) and multiverse (130 QA) are the two largest topics in the corpus; the 2023 vault has no physics category at all."}
{"label": "Reality", "definition": "What exists: realism, the reality of abstractions, and the criterion that an entity is real if it figures in our best explanations.", "topics": ["reality", "realism", "physicalism", "abstractions"], "rationale": "Listed in Randy's own 'Topics - Important' set but absent from the vault's categories; The Reality of Abstractions is a core BOI theme."}
{"label": "Constructor Theory", "definition": "The reformulation of fundamental physics in terms of which transformations are possible or impossible, and why.", "topics": ["constructor-theory", "universal-constructor"], "rationale": "46 QA items and a major post-2012 research program; postdates the themes captured in the 2023 vault."}
{"label": "Morality", "definition": "Objective moral knowledge: moral problems are soluble, moral progress is real, and moral explanations can be criticized and improved like any other.", "topics": ["morality"], "rationale": "67 QA items; a first-tier Deutsch theme with no home among the 2023 categories."}
{"label": "Children and Education", "definition": "Taking Children Seriously: non-coercive education, children as full people and knowledge creators.", "topics": ["children", "education", "tcs", "coercion"], "rationale": "41 TCS posts joined the corpus plus education (47 QA); nothing in the 2023 vault covers it."}
{"label": "Beauty and Aesthetics", "definition": "Objective aesthetic truth: why flowers are beautiful, beauty as hard-to-forge signaling, art as a domain of progress.", "topics": ["beauty", "aesthetics"], "rationale": "A distinctive Deutsch position (BOI ch. 14) discussed across many interviews; absent from the 2023 categories."}
